<title>BANGLADESH: Chittagong port handles 21,917 tonnes of cargo.</title>
<headline>Chittagong port handles 21,917 tonnes of cargo.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's main Chittagong port handled 21,917 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours ending at 1.0 p.m. (0700 GMT) on Sunday compared with 16,218 tonnes in the same period on Thursday, port officials said.</p>
<p>Break bulk and containerised cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					  Sunday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo		     3,421	 5,162</p>
<p>    Import Cargo		    18,496	11,056</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels expected to unload at Chittagong Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity		     Tonnes     Ships	  Berthing</p>
<p>    Granular Super Phosphate  10,000     Nanping Shan  18/8</p>
<p>    Cement			   24,000    Star Glory    18/8</p>
<p>    Cement			   18,000    Alinda	  18/8</p>
<p>    Vehicles			    689    Pacific Aries 18/8</p>
<p>    Rock Sulphate		  16,500    Aspidoforos   20/8</p>
<p>    Crude Degum Soyabean Oil   11,500    Normar Spirit 20/8</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
